#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078249 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078537 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eaac3fe1-285b-57ba-956b-66eaf51ded7e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Trigonometric Ratios Given a Triangle with Integer Side Lengths"}] :question/id #uuid "65c52289-9781-5418-b8c6-fb7693aad674" :question/math-academy-id "e-3240" :question/problem "Find $\\sin{\\theta},$ $\\cos{\\theta},$ and $\\tan{\\theta}$ for the triangle below.\n\n![](images/ed/ed11931671711d754241c84981e7cebf12f04bdae56a1c8b26a194a6bf44b7ca.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember the acronym \"SOH-CAH-TOA.\"\n\n- The sine of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the hypotenuse (S-O-H). Relative to the angle $\\theta,$ the opposite side is $\\overline{AC},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overline{BC}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\sin{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AC}{BC} = \\dfrac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\n- The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H). Relative to the angle $\\theta,$ the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overline{BC}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\cos{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AB}{BC} = \\dfrac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\n- The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to the angle $\\theta,$ the opposite side is $\\overline{AC},$ and the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\tan{\\theta} = \\dfrac{AC}{AB} = \\dfrac{3}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078251 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078539 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6359c90-3e3e-54f3-a66b-c8f69058a3a3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "e012dbd0-341b-5f01-a670-539c472471bb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3243" :question/problem "Given that $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{1}{4},$ find the value of $x.$\n\n![](images/f8/f8affbac78c75000d7bbbc8c15508252f7bea0270fdf6cc9c5e5244eb89b505d.png)" :question/worked-solution "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A).\n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta,$ the length of the opposite side is $x-1,$ and the length of the adjacent side is $2x.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{x-1}{2x} \\\\ 2x & =4(x-1) \\\\ 2x & =4x-4 \\\\ 2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078253 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078538 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c8132c-18c7-5250-a68e-68500bdb926e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Trigonometric Ratio Given a Triangle with Non-Integer Side Lengths"}] :question/id #uuid "c9ac49b1-04df-5cf0-bd38-3bc5b044b612" :question/math-academy-id "e-3245" :question/problem "In the right triangle $\\triangle ABC,$ the angle $\\angle A$ is a right angle, and the side lengths are $AB=2,$ $AC=\\sqrt{5},$ and $BC=3.$ Find $\\tan B.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's illustrate the given triangle.\n\n![](images/4e/4e4e2005e31716a09953aed9054cc5796ee915d41d5a9020042984b348e3b743.png)\n\nThe tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). Relative to $\\angle B,$ the opposite side is $\\overline{AC},$ and the adjacent side is $\\overline{AB}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\tan{B} &= \\dfrac{AC}{AB} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078255 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078540 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcbd6c22-13de-5a61-90b0-38bd478b4f2f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Trigonometric Function Using a Calculator"}] :question/id #uuid "81f7e0c1-99bf-5feb-9db2-745595a8b613" :question/math-academy-id "e-3247" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\cos\\left(50^\\circ\\right).$ Round the answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Using a calculator, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({50}^{∘}) & =0.64278...≈0.64,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078539 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6359c90-3e3e-54f3-a66b-c8f69058a3a3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54889477-a9fd-55c0-bd74-a943ba627d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561793} {:answer/id #uuid "631d6b33-926c-57c5-b3f1-ecb40b7e66be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561823} {:answer/id #uuid "917c3b75-1fb5-5141-b5d8-7f8a0c0b3eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561945} {:answer/id #uuid "b9deb636-6da1-5752-81cc-bc8451faac84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562056} {:answer/id #uuid "eefa9668-3ca9-547b-8410-3ba4c6bf019c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "917c3b75-1fb5-5141-b5d8-7f8a0c0b3eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561945} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdb72b5e-3640-52fa-95f4-ecdf6dcc4bd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e934f97-b3fe-53b9-be38-8426c7f7fdb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-121889" :question/problem "![](images/d0/d08a4d0946265ba1314831913b7c31de68fb59845fca42b2b79707c04dbd827c.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{8},$ the value of $x$ is" :question/worked-solution "The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H).\n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta ,$ the length of the adjacent side is $\\frac{7}{4}x+29,$ and the length of the hypotenuse is $7x+17.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4}x+29)}{7x+17} \\\\ 5(7x+17) & =8(\\frac{7}{4}x+29) \\\\ 35x+85 & =14x+232 \\\\ 21x & =147 \\\\ x & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078539 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6359c90-3e3e-54f3-a66b-c8f69058a3a3" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11d8f7cd-76de-5c8f-a7e1-4dc87b73db86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561637} {:answer/id #uuid "162d545d-4902-5d83-958a-e5ca68604c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561649} {:answer/id #uuid "4ede53c3-8e86-5289-a1d5-d65a3304ee50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561784} {:answer/id #uuid "685428e6-feeb-5203-b19c-cb5a6c3ab22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561842} {:answer/id #uuid "84a45b8e-205b-58fa-b8a7-69ea3b9a7a7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "685428e6-feeb-5203-b19c-cb5a6c3ab22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561842} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd9dfa97-5736-54f0-a836-6e83defce220" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "07f55725-512f-52ff-845b-7dcde64b9b62" :question/math-academy-id "q-121893" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e23e1c8331838c31bbf9943d95a313a84ff1a341e9200d78a66c2543fe00cc6d.png)\n\nIf $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{15}{12},$ then $x=$" :question/worked-solution "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A). \n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta ,$ the length of the opposite side is $6x-5,$ and the length of the adjacent side is $4x.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}} \\\\ \\frac{15}{12} & =\\frac{6x-5}{4x} \\\\ 60x & =72x-60 \\\\ 12x & =60 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078540 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcbd6c22-13de-5a61-90b0-38bd478b4f2f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Trigonometric Function Using a Calculator"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8786983-46a5-5513-b721-9846e247b148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.999" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8786983-46a5-5513-b721-9846e247b148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.999" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562156} :answer-field/id #uuid "accb383e-3441-5045-89e0-bc4d077184d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8784f120-baa9-5904-bf25-48701c5330e9" :question/mat